#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# shortest

#% text
# `shortest(p)` makes the runs and repetitions inside the pattern `p` take as little as possible first (string patterns are greedy by default).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
string_cases("0111011110", shortest(repeated("1")))
#% output
#= ["1", "1", "1", "1", "1", "1", "1"]

#% cell
string_replace("011110A010", shortest(string_expression("0", __, "0")) :> "x")
#% output
#= "xAx"

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# In a term pattern `shortest(xs__)` makes the run as short as possible before the unmarked runs are considered; `shortest(p, k)` gives it priority `k` among the marked runs (higher first).

#% cell
rewrite([a, b, c, d], [x__, shortest(y__)] :> [x, y])
#% output
#= [[a, b, c], [d]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `longest`, `string_expression`, `string_cases`
